# Docs vault

The living project notes are the Obsidian vault in `docs/`. Open that folder as the vault. Start from `docs/Home.md`.

After a crucial task (new behavior, architecture change, project layout, build setup, or a decision that later README text will depend on):

- Update the existing note for the affected project or component.
- Add a decision note under `docs/01 Decisions/` when the change records a choice, and link it from `Decision index`.
- Add one dated line to `docs/Log.md`.
- Leave the root `README` unwritten until the notes are ready to be turned into it. `docs/README outline.md` is only the outline.

Write notes in English. Keep class names, paths, and API names in the form used in the code. Do not duplicate long code listings; link the source path and describe the behavior.
